// symbols.12da - vertex symbols the way 12d Model 15 writes them (PLAN.MD
// 20.2 slice 2). Hand-written; the forms and field order are those of the
// real archives this reader was learned from.
//
//   - four surveyed points, each a `symbol_value` or a one-block
//     `symbol_data`, the string's own linestyle "0" beside the symbol's
//   - a fence line with a post at every vertex (`symbol_data`, one block per
//     vertex), which Katana keeps and writes back but does not draw
//   - a point in a linestyle that carries no symbol at all
//
// Coordinates are MGA2020 zone 56, beside all_geometries.12da.

// A hand-written 12da inherits the format's CURRENT BREAKLINE TYPE, whose
// default is `point` (commands, 1.4.4), and `breakline point` means the
// string's vertices are separate POINTS rather than a line through them. 12d
// writes the flag on every string it exports and leaves nothing to the
// default; this says it once for the strings below that do not, so that a
// string meaning a line is read as one. A string that wants points overrides
// it with `breakline point` of its own.
breakline line
string super {
  name      "PSMH"
  chainage  0
  breakline point
  colour    "yellow"
  style     "0"
  closed 0
  data_3d {
    502010.000 6960010.000 31.25
  }
  symbol_value {
    style     "SEWR Manhole Cover"
    colour    "yellow"
    size      1
    rotation  0
    offset    0
    raise     0
  }
}

